From 86d01e947126e81b2debae4a3d7fe14517e29d9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 07:24:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: judge each back-away grid on its own

The back-away step of borg_caution() looks at the eight grids around the
borg for a safer one to step to.  Two slips cut that search short:

- adjacent_monster was set inside the grid loop and never cleared, so
  once one candidate grid was next to a monster, every later candidate
  was skipped as well;
- a known trap on one candidate grid ended the whole scan ('break')
  instead of skipping just that grid.

Since the grids are scanned in a fixed order (south first), a hurt borg
whose southern neighbour was next to the monster, or held a trap, never
backed away even with a safe grid to the north.

Clear the flag for each candidate and skip a trapped grid with
'continue'.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#155.

(cherry picked from commit df5361ad5cc3977c75a86061ad0d944568885d77)
---
 src/borg/borg-caution.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-caution.c b/src/borg/borg-caution.c
index 19cdf5c0d..43a99dd0b 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-caution.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-caution.c
@@ -1719,7 +1719,7 @@ bool borg_caution(void)
 
             /* Mega-Hack -- skip traps XXX XXX XXX */
             if (ag->trap && !ag->glyph)
-                break;
+                continue;
 
             /* If i was here last round and 3 rounds ago, suggesting a "bounce"
              */
@@ -1736,6 +1736,7 @@ bool borg_caution(void)
              * Skip this grid if it is adjacent to a monster.  He will just hit
              * me when I land on that grid.
              */
+            adjacent_monster = false;
             for (ii = 1; ii < borg_kills_nxt; ii++) {
                 borg_kill *kill;
 
